app servers, which handle services, authentication, and data persistence",[287,295,296,299],{},[290,297,298],{},"Supporting services"," — Any additional infrastructure your application depends on",[280,301,302,303,307],{},"The Docker Compose configuration lives in ",[304,305,306],"code",{},"deployment\u002Fdocker-compose\u002F"," and can be started with a single command to give you a production-like environment for local testing.",[275,309,311],{"id":310},"staging","Staging",[280,313,314],{},"The staging environment runs on Kubernetes and mirrors production as closely as possible:",[284,316,317,320,323],{},[287,318,319],{},"Kubernetes-based deployment using Helm charts",[287,321,322],{},"Separate data stores from production for safe migration testing",[287,324,325],{},"Accessible to the development team for pre-production verification",[275,327,329],{"id":328},"production","Production",[280,331,332],{},"Production is a full Kubernetes deployment managed through Helm charts:",[284,334,335,338,341,344],{},[287,336,337],{},"High-availability configuration with appropriate replica counts",[287,339,340],{},"Managed data persistence",[287,342,343],{},"TLS termination and ingress configuration",[287,345,346],{},"Monitoring and observability integration",{"title":348,"searchDepth":349,"depth":349,"links":350},"",2,[351,352,353],{"id":277,"depth":349,"text":278},{"id":310,"depth":349,"text":311},{"id":328,"depth":349,"text":329},"Development, staging, and production environment configuration.","md",null,{},{"icon":145},{"title":142,"description":354},"Kes_lOY0LZu4JLIbv2hKrCRGPiZgotXQ9WEbXNvLURY",[362,364],{"title":137,"path":138,"stem":139,"description":363,"icon":140,"children":-1},"The Kinotic deployment pipeline from development to production.",{"title":147,"path":148,"stem":149,"description":365,"icon":6,"children":-1},"How a git push to your project's repository becomes a running deployment.",1792981942289]